Subject: [PATCH] Align private VM tracing records for instrumented C accesses

Use the ring buffer's existing eight-byte record layout when alignment
instrumentation is enabled. Four-byte x86 records otherwise expose
misaligned ftrace_entry members to the C compiler even though x86 hardware
accepts those instructions. Both record readers and writers already support
the eight-byte layout; no instrumentation is disabled.

--- a/kernel/trace/ring_buffer.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/ring_buffer.c
@@ -161,7 +161,8 @@
 #define RB_MAX_SMALL_DATA	(RB_ALIGNMENT * RINGBUF_TYPE_DATA_TYPE_LEN_MAX)
 #define RB_EVNT_MIN_SIZE	8U	/* two 32bit words */
 
-#ifndef CONFIG_HAVE_64BIT_ALIGNED_ACCESS
+#if !defined(CONFIG_HAVE_64BIT_ALIGNED_ACCESS) && \
+	!defined(CONFIG_UBSAN_ALIGNMENT)
 # define RB_FORCE_8BYTE_ALIGNMENT	0
 # define RB_ARCH_ALIGNMENT		RB_ALIGNMENT
 #else
